  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Arsenious sulphide is -ve charged colloid. Hence, cation having maximum positive charge will be most effective for coagulation. (Hardy Schulz rule)<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> (coagulating power)",
    "image": null
